  "checks": [
    "Authorized infrastructure provisioning reconciles the separate publication table without installing a future calculation definition.",
    "Frozen actor/time, owner, original policy, schema identities, placement and resource generations; owned models must share the physical namespace.",
    "Canonical bounded JSON rejects duplicate fields, trailing tokens, fractional/string integral metadata, unknown or corrupted state and checksum/identity mismatch.",
    "STAGING/APPLYING/RESTORING counts and cursors persist monotonically; 100% counts are not terminal publication acknowledgement.",
    "Checkpoint updates compare tenant/model/target/fingerprint, original immutable intent checksum, sequence and previous checkpoint checksum.",
    "Real Calcite insert/update and caller marker writes roll back atomically; new connections recover committed checkpoints.",
    "Duplicate operation IDs and stale/foreign updates cannot replace the original intent; other tenants cannot read it.",
    "Failed batches retain progress; restoration and terminal cancellation remain distinct. Journal cancellation and write-fence consumption commit or roll back together.",
    "Shared production Calcite catalog retains physical dialect, temporal type system, UTC and microsecond precision."
  ],
  "correctedFindings": [
    "The first UPDATE passed a raw Timestamp; both databases rejected the resulting integer. Journal updates now use the shared RecordSqlParameters encoder.",
    "The existing database fixture used a default Calcite catalog, losing microseconds and UTC semantics. RuntimeRecordCatalog now shares the production configuration with the real transaction fixtures; the precision assertions pass unchanged."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is the target intent/checkpoint journal foundation; no public formula publication has been enabled.",
    "Aggregate staged results and undo values, actual backfill/restore workers, ordinary read/write/replay/snapshot maintenance admission and schema/resource-management exclusion remain to implement.",
    "Current transaction tests use marker rows to establish journal/target atomicity; they are not final business aggregate backfill/undo acceptance.",
    "APP trusted projection, final UI progress, designer/runtime integration and the complete 176-entry business matrix remain incomplete.",
    "This batch has not been deployed; introduce the infrastructure upgrade before enabling any runtime admission reads of the new journal."
  ],
